# Geospatial Analytics & Spatial Data Engineering Pipeline 🌍📊

An end-to-end computing pipeline designed to process, analyze, and model large-scale spatial data, transitioning from traditional rows-and-columns tabular structures into multi-dimensional location intelligence.

## 📌 Project Overview:-

* Goal:- Extract location-based insights by evaluating where events happen alongside what happens.
* Architecture:- Hybrid vector and raster ingestion engine supported by localized spatial databases.
* Business Impact:- Automates proximity risk assessment and high-traffic site selection modeling.

## 🔄 Technical Workflow:-

* Data Structuring:- Modeled geographic primitives into Vector (Points/Lines/Polygons) and Raster grids.
* Cloud-Native Optimization:- Integrated GeoParquet and Cloud-Optimized GeoTIFF (COG) for file streaming.
* Spatial Relational Joins:- Executed proximity, containment, and intersection queries using coordinate overlays.

## ⚙️ Geospatial Technology Core Matrix:-

* QGIS:- Multi-layer map visualization and visual data processing auditing.
* PostGIS:- Enterprise spatial database indexing to query millions of coordinates using spatial SQL.
* GeoPandas:- Vector geometry analysis, geocoding pipelines, and operations inside Python dataframes.
* Apache Sedona:- Distributed big data scaling for cloud-based geospatial analytics pipelines.

## 🧰 Tech Stack:-

* Core Languages:- Python, SQL
* Gis Toolsets:- QGIS, PostGIS, GeoPandas, Apache Sedona
* Data Formats:-GeoParquet, Cloud-Optimized GeoTIFF (COG), NetCDF, LiDAR 3D Points

